/github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/issues/4#issuecomment-6981335805\n\nQuestion: do the six nested receipt consumers and one direct archive consumer mutate their freshly returned prerequisite graphs during one original saved-archive read?\n\nThis draft adds a read-only wrapper, partial receipts, strict seven-call and full graph/semantic witnesses, plus synthetic order, mutation and failure-restoration tests. The original reader and all its validations remain in place. No archived audit, cache, training, reference construction, savings estimate, forecast admission or stronger-play claim has run or been made.\n\nExact source head: `dd53e9904d8d31cb0407a9662f0880f851907b7a`. Both clean local bases pass 5,582 tests (71 skipped, 150 deselected) with Ruff, formatting and strict mypy on 837 files. Both complete 69-file optional scopes pass 2,491 tests on locked Python 3.11.17/NumPy 2.4.6 and Python 3.12.15/NumPy 2.5.4. The prior 458-file scientific source fingerprint remains `b475bfefb92963f25458d97260264743ff4d751b4513c307529742eaf10fc97d`. Installed OpenSpiel 2.0.2 Apache-2.0 license bytes match the pinned SHA-256. Precommit dirty-checkout import failures and an earlier incomplete 68-file optional pass are retained, not counted as qualification.\n\nPending: hosted CI on this source head; publish verified six-role source checks; then run two bounded actual archived reads and publish raw data before any report; final exact-head qualification and history-preserving merge. A pass from this audit would establish only consumer nonmutation in one read, not safe reuse.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T15:43:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T15:43:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"4cc36a7042e83bd3e044c5e571b54998ecfb9480","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"jimmy-sim:research/receipt-consumer-mutation","ref":"research/receipt-consumer-mutation","repo":{"id":1